{
  "$comment": "The native libraries the iOS and Android builds add on top of the npm packages (scripts/licenses.mjs puts them in Настройки → Лицензи). Each: its licence's text (a file here, from the project's own repository) or, under Apache-2.0, its copyright holder and that licence's one full text; `match` is what it is in a build — a framework or bundle in the iOS .app, a .so or a META-INF/*.version in the Android .apk — for `npm run native-notices -- <.app|.apk>`, which names whatever a new build holds that nothing here covers. `covered` is what the npm packages' notices already cover (their native code ships with them).",
